  "summary": "Headline metadata indicates Tata Consultancy Services (TCS) is under investigation in the United States over allegations it dismissed American employees while retaining H-1B visa holders. The supplied feed contains only metadata and no full article text. The probe could involve federal labor and immigration regulators and may have implications for compliance, corporate hiring practices, and TCS's reputation in the US.",
  "content": "The available item carries the headline that Tata Consultancy Services (TCS) is under investigation in the United States over allegations it fired American employees while retaining H-1B visa holders. The provided feed contains only metadata and no full article text.\\n\\nAccording to the headline and sparse metadata, the probe appears to concern employment and visa practices. Such investigations are typically handled by federal labor and immigration agencies and may examine whether an employer unlawfully preferred visa holders over domestic workers or violated hiring and termination rules.\\n\\nIf substantiated, the allegations could have consequences for TCS's compliance obligations, potential penalties, and reputation in the US market. The case could also prompt closer scrutiny of how multinational IT firms use H-1B workers relative to American staff.\\n\\nBecause the source content supplied here lacks the full story and supporting details, readers should treat the headline as preliminary. Follow-up reporting from established news outlets or statements from regulators and TCS will be needed to confirm the scope, parties involved, and outcomes.",
