  "markdown_content": "## Headline\\n\\n> \u201cTata Consultancy Services (TCS) is under investigation in the United States over allegations it fired American employees while retaining H-1B visa holders.\u201d\\n\\n## Incident details\\n\\nAccording to the headline and sparse metadata, the probe appears to concern employment and visa practices. Such investigations are typically handled by federal labor and immigration agencies and may examine whether an employer unlawfully preferred visa holders over domestic workers or violated hiring and termination rules.\\n\\n* Agencies that commonly handle these matters include federal labor and immigration authorities (for example, the U.S. Department of Labor and related enforcement bodies).\\n* The investigation, as suggested by the headline, focuses on potential disparities in treatment between American employees and H-1B visa holders.\\n\\n## Potential implications\\n\\nIf substantiated, the allegations could have consequences for TCS\u2019s compliance obligations, potential penalties, and reputation in the U.S. market. The case could also prompt closer scrutiny of how multinational IT firms use H-1B workers relative to American staff.\\n\\n* Possible regulatory penalties or enforcement actions\\n* Increased compliance and reporting requirements\\n* Reputational impact and heightened public and regulatory scrutiny\\n\\n## Limitations and next steps\\n\\nBecause the source content supplied here lacks the full story and supporting details, readers should treat the headline as preliminary. Follow-up reporting from established news outlets or statements from regulators and TCS will be needed to confirm the scope, parties involved, and outcomes.\\n\\n* Look for official statements from TCS and relevant U.S. agencies\\n* Await detailed reporting that cites documents, filings, or spokespeople for confirmation",
